  "id": "COMPOUND:33929 - PROTEIN:1381",
  "verbalization": "Donnaienin is implicated in the regulation of Beclin-1 through multiple pathways, with the compound acting as a target for several enzymes, including Stromelysin-1 and DNA polymerase I. The evidence suggests that Donnaienin may modulate Beclin-1 through the inhibition of these enzymes, which in turn could influence downstream processes involving autophagy. The presence of a common target, (1S,2R,3S,4R,5R)-2,3,4-trihydroxy-N-octyl-6-oxa-8-azabicyclo[3.2.1]octane-8-carbothioamide, which is a known inhibitor of Beclin-1, further supports the notion that Donnaienin may interact with Beclin-1 via this pathway. The integration of multiple targets and the shared mechanism of action highlight a potential role for Donnaienin in regulating autophagic pathways, particularly through the inhibition of enzymes involved in the degradation of cellular components. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Donnaienin and Beclin-1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
